  "body": "podliner v2.3.0\n\na light theme.\n\n## new\n\n- **light theme.** `:theme light` or `--theme light` switches to a light background with dark text. `t` cycles through it like the other themes and the choice is kept across restarts. it covers the whole ui, including menus, dialogs, the help browser and the log view. the cursor and the progress bar are blue and there is no yellow anywhere.\n\n  terminals only give podliner their 16 colours, so how it looks depends on your palette. the colours are picked so text stays readable (at least 4.5:1) in the xterm, linux console, windows terminal, macOS terminal and gnome terminal defaults. in a palette where white and light grey are the same colour it will look flat.\n"
